  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.15,
      "end": 2.108,
      "text": "A signal crosses the universe,",
      "beat": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 2.108,
      "end": 5.372,
      "text": "then vanishes in milliseconds.\nWhat could make it?",
      "beat": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 5.552,
      "end": 8.273,
      "text": "Astronomers call these\nfast radio bursts.",
      "beat": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 8.273,
      "end": 13.648,
      "text": "Brief radio flashes, some from galaxies\nmillions or billions of light-years away.",
      "beat": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 13.828,
      "end": 16.398,
      "text": "The first was reported in 2007.",
      "beat": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 16.398,
      "end": 21.703,
      "text": "CHIME has detected thousands;\na small number are seen to repeat.",
      "beat": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 21.883,
      "end": 26.24,
      "text": "In 2020, a burst from a magnetar\nin our galaxy gave a vital clue.",
      "beat": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 26.24,
      "end": 30.262,
      "text": "A magnetar is a neutron star with\nan extreme magnetic field.",
      "beat": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 30.442,
      "end": 32.013,
      "text": "Another burst studied in Nature",
      "beat": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 32.013,
      "end": 35.56,
      "text": "appears to have come from the magnetic\nregion close to a neutron star.",
      "beat": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 35.74,
      "end": 37.897,
      "text": "But the mystery is not solved.",
      "beat": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 37.897,
      "end": 42.931,
      "text": "How are these flashes generated?\nDo all share the same kind of source?",
      "beat": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 43.111,
      "end": 46.052,
      "text": "Some repeat. Others have only\nbeen seen once.",
      "beat": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 46.052,
      "end": 49.58,
      "text": "Are they different \u2014 or are we\nmissing the next flash?",
      "beat": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 49.76,
      "end": 52.192,
      "text": "For now, the universe\nkeeps sending clues.",
      "beat": 8
    },
    {
      "start": 52.192,
      "end": 55.841,
      "text": "Save this video, and subscribe\nfor the next unsolved discovery.",
      "beat": 8
